{
  "id": "u06-l01",
  "unit": "u06-bazaar",
  "title": "How much?",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "To ask a price, say **দাম কত?** (*dam koto?*) — literally 'price how-much?'. Like কী in Unit 1, **কত** sits where the answer will go, so no word order change is needed.\n\nTo say *whose* price, add the genitive ending: **-র** after a vowel (এটা → **এটার**, 'of this') and **-এর** after a consonant (ইলিশ → **ইলিশের**, 'of the hilsa'). So **ইলিশের দাম কত?** = 'How much is the hilsa?'.\n\nThe ending **-এ** means 'at / in': **বাজারে** = 'at the market'. Location needs **আছি / আছে**: **আমি বাজারে আছি** 'I am at the market'.\n\n**Culture:** in a Bangladeshi bazaar you call the shopkeeper **ভাই** (brother) or **মামা** (uncle) rather than 'excuse me'.",
